      "id": "visible-baseline",
      "response_lines": [
        11,
        47
      ],
      "classification": "valid_baseline",
      "reason": "The coprime power-map/line-circle proof covers all active supports. The (z−1)(z−ζ) example satisfies the prime-power hypotheses and has all coefficients nonzero because N is odd."
    },
    {
      "id": "finite-abelian-zero-sets",
      "response_lines": [
        51,
        177
      ],
      "classification": "valid_R3_structure",
      "reason": "After dividing by χ1, u and v descend to H=G/(ker u∩ker v) and jointly separate points; χ1 itself is never falsely assumed to descend. Three active coefficients admit at most two H zeros by the unit-torus line argument. For two selected points the cross-product kernel has all entries nonzero exactly when their ratio is in Ω. The singleton construction and the finite excluded-t parameterization are valid, as are every binary fiber and all single-term cases. This is a full inverse zero-set classification on arbitrary finite abelian groups."
    },
    {
      "id": "v4-exception-and-coefficient-strata",
      "response_lines": [
        179,
        266
      ],
      "classification": "valid_additional_structure",
      "reason": "Checked H1,H2,H3 are proper with pairwise identity intersections. If their union exhausts H, each is nontrivial; products (1,α)(β,1) force both off-axis coordinates to be −1 and then force the diagonal element to be (−1,−1). Thus the sole Ω-empty image is V4. The double-zero count m|Ω|/2 and binary parameter counts follow without overcounting. Although 2k is unavailable with three active terms in V4, a binary kernel has 2k points, so the asserted all-support zero-count set is still correct."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluation-rank",
      "response_lines": [
        268,
        296
      ],
      "classification": "valid_additional_theorem",
      "reason": "Distinct H points give nonproportional normalized rows. Three or more zeros can only be caused by a binary function, hence rank deficiency is exactly containment in an Hi coset, and its rank is two. Empty, singleton and two-point cases agree with rank-nullity."
    },
    {
      "id": "cyclic-specialization-and-reconstruction",
      "response_lines": [
        298,
        450
      ],
      "classification": "valid_R3_structure",
      "reason": "The common kernel is μ_g and the quotient is cyclic, excluding V4. This yields the exact arbitrary-N extrema, all achievable cardinalities and necessary-and-sufficient universal two-zero criterion. The forward formula obtains the two circle candidates, then U^m=V^m=1 and U^e=V^d are sufficient by sd+te+ℓm=1; x=U^sV^t is unique and its g-th roots are exactly the original μ_N fiber. The binary condition and count use the correct image μ_(N/δ)."
    },
    {
      "id": "submitted-files-and-verification-claim",
